      "post_subject": "Emulsion covered object.",
      "content_md": "Well, my first attempt did not work so well.\n\nI took a couple of very shiny glazed porcelain drawer knobs and a couple of other white object and coated them with DCG. I then exposed and processed them. I was hoping to get some type of reflection colors off of them. I could bearly see some colors on only one. I suspect I should see a gold reflection off the white knob if it works as planned and then as the angle changes the color should shift.\n\nI will have to try this again.",
